WEBVTT


00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:04.740
Watch as we knit our
Prickly Pear Pullover.

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:09.870
I'm sure you could knit a more exciting
version of this sweater, but to keep

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:15.510
things simple, I knit a plain stockinette
version and one color and followed the

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:16.590
pattern exactly.

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:20.250
The sweater is knit in just 5 pieces.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:22.260
Knit the back.

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:25.770
It's just a rectangle,
but follow the pattern.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:30.060
Place the markers and
scrap off as instructed.

00:00:32.409 --> 00:00:33.700
Knit the front.

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:39.580
The neck line shaping isn't hard, but plan
to knit your front on a day when you're

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:42.340
fresh and there aren't any distractions.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:46.090
Join one shoulder.

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:50.950
Knit a plain rolled neck band.

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:53.920
Remember, we're keeping this simple.

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:57.940
Then join the other shoulder.

00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:03.080
Knit the sleeves from the top down.

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:13.940
Try to knit both sleeves
and one knitting session.

00:01:14.539 --> 00:01:19.700
Again, choose a day with no distractions,
so both sleeves end up the same length.

00:01:20.675 --> 00:01:27.395
Block your sweater, find a sunny spot,
sew up the seams, and hide the ends.

00:01:28.505 --> 00:01:31.414
And then take a photo
and share your success.

